(7472768, 1186339, 181847, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> NO HAZE!!!  I wonder if this was taken during the "Blue Hour"...Never knew about that until recently.  Very beautiful...where is it? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No, it was shot about 8:30AM. The morning was incredibly clear with absolutely no haze or humidity in the air.  <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: NO HAZE!!!  I wonder if this was taken during the "Blue Hour"...Never knew about that until recently.  Very beautiful...where is it?   No, it was shot about 8:30AM. The morning was incredibly clear with absolutely no haze or humidity in the air.  ', '2016-09-06 16:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7472793, 1186687, 43111, '<td valign="top">I knew this shot wouldn''t do well with the DPC crowd (not a criticism of the reviewers, just a matter of personal tastes) because of the "over-processed" HDR.  I decided to submit it anyway.  I am typically not a fan of that look myself, and I''m the first to admit this doesn''t look realistic.  But why does everything have to?  What I get from this is a sort of post-apocalyptic, end of the world feeling, and the processing was necessary for that.  A more conventionally processed image might be a nice picture of a dead tree, it just wasn''t what I was trying for here.  I didn''t want just a dead tree, I wanted something where you were looking for some radioactive mutant to be peering out from behind it.</td>', 'I knew this shot wouldn''t do well with the DPC crowd (not a criticism of the reviewers, just a matter of personal tastes) because of the "over-processed" HDR.  I decided to submit it anyway.  I am typically not a fan of that look myself, and I''m the first to admit this doesn''t look realistic.  But why does everything have to?  What I get from this is a sort of post-apocalyptic, end of the world feeling, and the processing was necessary for that.  A more conventionally processed image might be a nice picture of a dead tree, it just wasn''t what I was trying for here.  I didn''t want just a dead tree, I wanted something where you were looking for some radioactive mutant to be peering out from behind it.', '2016-09-06 17:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
